      "side": 1,
      "message": "PS1 had this assert and you can see [failures here](https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/try/win-dawn-rel/51568/overview). d3d12::Device::CreateZeroBuffer() runs from d3d12::Device::Initialize() after device mutex is created but it\u0027s not locked. The device mutex isn\u0027t really needed yet since device creation is single threaded. I think we could probably just lock the mutex or delay creating it to end of d3d12::Device::Initialize()?",
